31
00:01:37,250 --> 00:01:41,110
And also I wanted
my students to be

32
00:01:41,110 --> 00:01:46,030
not only information consumers,
but knowledge producers.

33
00:01:46,030 --> 00:01:48,310
You know, professors
write articles.

34
00:01:48,310 --> 00:01:53,380
And that's a big part of being
an academic, you write articles

35
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:55,240
and you want to publish them.

36
00:01:55,240 --> 00:02:01,970
And on the good day, you might
have a few people actually read

37
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:02,980
what you're writing.

38
00:02:02,980 --> 00:02:05,895
But when students write,
or people in general

39
00:02:05,895 --> 00:02:10,250
write on Wikipedia,
this work gets read.

40
00:02:10,250 --> 00:02:16,320
A small school in Israel, where
they speak Circassi-- they

41
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:20,200
speak Adyghe, which is the
language of Circassi people.

42
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:24,820
And these are eighth
grade students.

43
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:26,750
And because of
the work they did,

44
00:02:26,750 --> 00:02:29,260
we have a new language
Wikipedia that

45
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:32,310
just opened,
Wikipedia in Adyghe,

46
00:02:32,310 --> 00:02:33,680
and we are very proud of it.

47
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:39,050
So it goes to show what eighth
grade students can actually

48
00:02:39,050 --> 00:02:39,950
achieve.

49
00:02:39,950 --> 00:02:42,510
If you think about the
student perspective,

50
00:02:42,510 --> 00:02:46,960
the students learn
21st-century skills

51
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:49,980
of engaging with
the global community

52
00:02:49,980 --> 00:02:53,460
and writing for a
global audience,

53
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:57,065
learning crazy awesome
research skills.

54
00:02:57,065 --> 00:03:00,420

55
00:03:00,420 --> 00:03:03,220
At the same time, they
are benefiting the world.

56
00:03:03,220 --> 00:03:09,000
Wikipedia is very important
for us, because in this way

57
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
we can preserve our language.

58
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:18,530
For example, Armenian language
isn't widespread in different,

59
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:21,690
for example, countries
like English, Spanish.

60
00:03:21,690 --> 00:03:24,020
So in this way we
preserve our language,

61
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:25,810
we preserve our culture.

62
00:03:25,810 --> 00:03:28,050
[SPEAKING EGYPTIAN ARABIC]

63
00:03:28,050 --> 00:03:47,060

64
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:51,680
The collaboration between
Wikipedia and universities

65
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:55,300
has been established in
most of the major schools

66
00:03:55,300 --> 00:04:02,010
in the Czech Republic,
in many types of classes.

67
00:04:02,010 --> 00:04:07,280
And we're adding hundreds of
thousands of bytes each year,

68
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:13,250
which means hundreds of pages
each year, to Wikipedia.

69
00:04:13,250 --> 00:04:17,310
And in subjects that would
never be probably written

70
00:04:17,310 --> 00:04:23,290
by our volunteers because
they are very specific, expert

71
00:04:23,290 --> 00:04:24,510
knowledge.

72
00:04:24,510 --> 00:04:27,770
Teachers were eager to
learn about Wikipedia.

73
00:04:27,770 --> 00:04:30,420
And some of them were
reluctant, but when

74
00:04:30,420 --> 00:04:34,680
they learned that they could
edit and make a change,

75
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:37,050
I think that made a difference.

76
00:04:37,050 --> 00:04:40,900
They started editing,
creating new articles,

77
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:43,930
and now they have a
sense of belonging.

78
00:04:43,930 --> 00:04:46,410
They see that they
can contribute

79
00:04:46,410 --> 00:04:48,170
to knowledge-building.

80
00:04:48,170 --> 00:04:52,780
In Ukraine we have a
common task for students.

81
00:04:52,780 --> 00:04:57,480
It's just papers,
ordinary papers.

82
00:04:57,480 --> 00:05:02,680
They are not research papers
but a compilation of information

83
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:04,090
from different sources.

84
00:05:04,090 --> 00:05:08,950
Basically, it's just what
Wikipedia is all about.

85
00:05:08,950 --> 00:05:14,580
So I've got to know
that Wikipedia Education

86
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:16,740
Program in Ukraine
at that moment

87
00:05:16,740 --> 00:05:23,890
was all about replacing
that dull papers made only

88
00:05:23,890 --> 00:05:28,330
by students for their teachers,
with writing an article which

89
00:05:28,330 --> 00:05:31,000
is by a student to
the whole world.

90
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,960
I have a teaching background,
and Wikipedia in education

91
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:41,100
has always been that one project
that really combines education

92
00:05:41,100 --> 00:05:46,050
and teaching, and also
the digital tools and ICT

93
00:05:46,050 --> 00:05:48,830
that we're talking about
in education a lot.

94
00:05:48,830 --> 00:05:54,480
And I think of education as a
really big driver for change.

95
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:57,800
And if you combine that
with the power of Wikipedia,

96
00:05:57,800 --> 00:06:01,290
where you can really
allow students

97
00:06:01,290 --> 00:06:03,730
to have real world impact.

98
00:06:03,730 --> 00:06:14,119